1) To clone remote files into our local machine/editor
 -> git clone https://github.com/janaaloke4/test-repo.git
2) in terminal inorder to move next folder we use below command 
 -> cd <filename>
3) To view all the available file inside the repo we use below command
-> ls
4) To Check if there is/are any changes between our local repo and remote repo, 
 -> git status
 ---- Type of git status --------------( File change cycle: Add new changes -> Add/stagging area -> commit ) 
	1) Untracked :  new files that git doesnt yet track, ex: we created a new file in our local repo which not yet push into remote file
	2) modified  :  This status appear when we made any new changes on the existing file, but not yet pushed into remote file
	3) staged	 :  This appear when file is ready tobe committed ( Before commit)

5) To move our changes into stagged state 
 -> git add <fileName>  // Single file 
 -> git add .           // Add all changes at once
 
6) Once we add our changes it is now ready to commit.
 -> git commit -m "<Add your commit message >"
 
7) To upload local repo content into remote repo we have to push our chnages , then only it will visable in the remote side.
 -> git push origin main